# Docker build context exclusions.
# Keeps credentials out of the build context entirely and avoids uploading
# large, regenerable trees (node_modules, venvs, caches) on every build.
#
# NOTE: .dockerignore patterns are matched against the full path relative to
# the context root, so a bare `node_modules` only excludes a root-level one.
# Recursive exclusions need both the bare and the `**/` form.

# --- Credentials and secrets (never belong in a build context) ---
id_ed25519*
**/id_ed25519*
*.pem
**/*.pem
*.key
**/*.key
secrets/
**/secrets/
.env
.env.*
**/.env
**/.env.*

# --- VCS and agent/tooling metadata ---
.git
.gitignore
.github
.agents
.claude
.specify

# --- Dependency trees and build output (rebuilt inside the image) ---
node_modules
**/node_modules
.venv
**/.venv
frontend/dist
frontend/coverage

# --- Python caches and artifacts ---
__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.pyc
**/*.pyc
*.pyo
**/*.pyo
*.egg-info
**/*.egg-info
.pytest_cache
**/.pytest_cache
.mypy_cache
**/.mypy_cache
.ruff_cache
**/.ruff_cache
.coverage
**/.coverage
htmlcov
**/htmlcov

# --- Test/dev noise ---
*.log
**/*.log
playwright-report
**/playwright-report
test-results
**/test-results

# --- Docs and specs (not needed to build the app) ---
docs/
specs/
README.md
LICENSE
